## Resolved mutable: m-minimal-sensible-tree-distance-unconfirmed

Vegetation.js's own renderDistance (default 640, or cfg override) already IS the correct 'minimal sensible tree distance' -- it's the subsystem's own configured visibility bound (impostor tier draws all the way to renderDistance, D3 is only the mesh-to-impostor LOD switch, not a hard cutoff). No re-derivation needed: the actual bug was never the renderDistance VALUE being wrong, it's that THREE's camera.far (which vegetation's BVH frustum cull reads) was being driven by an unrelated, altitude-sensitive terrain-horizon formula instead of vegetation's own renderDistance. Live A/B (far=7662 vs 2000 vs 700, near=30 vs 0.1, all at a real vista pose) proves terrain/water/sky (drawn by mapspinner, separate GL pass) are visually UNAFFECTED by THREE's near/far entirely -- confirming the fix is to decouple THREE's camera.near/far from mapspinner's sync altogether, driven instead by a small fixed near + far = max(vegetation.renderDistance, rocks.renderDistance, grass.renderDistance)+margin.